# fp8_gemm_kernel.lm_head_dx's K loop runs 512 trips under its record,
# and its <block 4> only on those whose counter passes line 957's
# `setp.ge.u64 %p3, %rd55, %rd2`, read per trip as `k < 511`: 510
# trips x 256 threads x 96 CTAs = 12,533,760, as Nsight Compute
# measures. Its two `cp.async` lines, 979 and 985, are `@!P0 LDGSTS`,
# whose L2 sectors Nsight Compute miscounts, so the record keeps none
# for them (micro/ldgsts_p0.ptx, PLAN.md).
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/gluon/fp8_gemm_kernel.lm_head_dx.sm_89.ptx --ncu %fixtures/gluon/fp8_gemm_kernel.lm_head_dx.sm_89.ncu.json | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: <block 4>{{ +}}gluon_fp8.py:201{{ +}}16  <= 256 in <= 8 warps (k[gluon_fp8.py:173] < 511)
CHECK: <block 4>        confirmed     16 instructions, 10 with SASS, 8 agreeing
CHECK-NOT: line 973:
CHECK: $L__BB0_1
CHECK-NOT: contradicted
CHECK: measured L2 sectors of global accesses: 22 lines agree (10 exact, 12 within a range, 0 within a bound), 0 differ
